  {
    "id": "anno-hachinohe_upper_p040_right-09",
    "type": "Annotation",
    "body": [
      {
        "purpose": "transcribing",
        "value": "雜税金　壹萬二千六百六十　兩二分一朱"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "modern_jp_reading",
        "value": "雑税金　一万二千六百六十〔一字分空白〕両二分一朱／12,660りょう2ぶ1しゅ"
      },
      {
        "purpose": "english_translation",
        "value": "Miscellaneous taxes paid in gold: 12,660 ryō 2 bu 1 shu, as printed (2 bu 1 shu = 0.5625 ryō). FLAG, one character cell is blank in the print: the column runs on a regular 84-85 px pitch and the cell between 六十 and 兩 (y2240-2339) is clean paper, minimum grey value 184 against an ink threshold of 110, so nothing was set there. The figure also fails to reconcile with the 此米 line two columns to the left: 1,582.82031 koku x 8 ryō/koku = 12,662.5625 ryō exactly, two ryō more than printed. The likeliest explanation is a 二 dropped from 六十〔二〕 by the 1928 compositor. Recorded as printed; the discrepancy is left open rather than silently repaired."
      },
      {
        "purpose": "identifying",
        "value": "雜税金"
      }
    ],
    "target": {
